 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A group of elements with similar properties is called a family. Four families have special names:\n• group 1: the alkali metals (lithium, sodium, potassium …);\n• group 2: the alkaline earth metals (beryllium, magnesium, calcium …);\n• group 7: the halogens (fluorine, chlorine, bromine, iodine);\n• group 8 (or 0): the noble gases (helium, neon, argon, krypton …).\nThe elements of a family have the same number of outer electrons. Hydrogen is in group 1 but is not an alkali metal: it is a non-metal gas.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "z": 19
  },
  "problem": "Which family does potassium (atomic number {z}) belong to? Explain.",
  "steps": [
